        <param>
          <type>const double *</type>
          <declname>coordinates</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Point location test: bounding box test <formula id="55">$ X_{\min,i} \le x_i &lt; X_{\max,i} $</formula>, and for a distorted cell additionally <formula id="56">$ -1 \le \xi_i &lt; 1 $</formula> for the parametric coordinates of <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_cells_1_1_lagrangian_cell_geometry_1ab8d88cbe9f44623e41d085b21affb8fa" kindref="member">findReferenceCoordinate()</ref>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Both tests are half-open, so that a point on a face shared by two cells belongs to exactly one of them; consequently, a point exactly on the upper boundary of the whole mesh belongs to no cell. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">coordinates</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Point coordinates (nDim values). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><computeroutput>true</computeroutput> if the point is inside the cell. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
