        <name>findReferenceCoordinate</name>
        <qualifiedname>Marmot::Discretizations::Cells::LagrangianCellGeometry::findReferenceCoordinate</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_cells_1_1_lagrangian_cell_geometry_1af5955fd949216affbae2658e25ced5de" kindref="member">XiSized</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>coord</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Inverse isoparametric map <formula id="57">$ \boldsymbol{\xi}(\boldsymbol{X}) $</formula>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Starts from the affine map of the bounding box, <formula id="58">$ \xi_i = 2\,(X_i - \tfrac12(X_{\max,i}+X_{\min,i}))/(X_{\max,i}-X_{\min,i}) $</formula>, which is exact for an axis-aligned box-shaped cell, and applies Newton&apos;s method,  <formula id="59">$ \boldsymbol{\xi} \leftarrow \boldsymbol{\xi} + \boldsymbol{J}^{-1}(\boldsymbol{X} - \sum_A
N_A(\boldsymbol{\xi})\boldsymbol{X}_A) $</formula>, until the residual is below <formula id="60">$ 10^{-12} $</formula> times the diagonal of the bounding box. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">coord</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Physical coordinates. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Parametric coordinates <formula id="61">$ \boldsymbol{\xi} $</formula>. </para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>std::runtime_error</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>if Newton&apos;s method does not converge within 20 iterations. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
